6. Third-party components and other programs

Third-Party Components are licensed under their own terms, which are listed
or referenced in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. Those terms, not this Licence, apply
to the Third-Party Components, and nothing in this Licence limits any right
those terms give You.

Other programs in the KrakenSDR suite that carry a different licence (in
particular the Heimdall receiver server in the heimdall_v2 folder and the GNU
Radio module in the gr-krakensdr_v2 folder, both under the GNU General Public
License version 3 or later) are separate works and are not part of the
Software. The Software communicates with them over network connections.

Not part of the Software either: the plugin SDK (the plugins/sdk folder and
plugins/SDK.md) and the Windows helpers in the win folder, which are under the
MIT License (plugins/sdk/LICENSE); and every decoder plugin whose folder
(plugins/<id>) holds a LICENSE file of its own - plugins/ism, under the GNU
General Public License version 2 or later, and plugins/flarm, under the GNU
General Public License version 3. Such a plugin is a
separate program: the Software starts it as a process of its own and
exchanges data with it through pipes, and it is built without the plugin
library or other parts of the Software. It is licensed only under the terms
in its folder.

Software that You obtain and install separately (for example voice codecs,
speech-recognition models or an AI assistant) is under its own terms. You are
responsible for having the rights, including any patent rights, needed to
obtain and use it.


